# 2 Stack
story += [P('1. Project in one minute','Title1'),P('Assurance &amp; Gestion des Sinistres is a semantic-web insurance workspace. Staff manage insured people, contracts, claims, experts and damages in one React application. Express validates requests and creates fixed SPARQL operations. Apache Jena Fuseki stores and queries RDF in TDB2. The OWL file supplies the domain vocabulary; application metadata tracks changes without editing that source file.'),P('Why this stack fits','Title2')]
story += [table([
['Choice','Role in this project','Reason it fits'],
['React 19 + TypeScript','Responsive pages, forms, tables, chatbot and route-level modules.','Reusable UI and typed client/server contracts help keep five related modules consistent.'],
['Vite 7 + npm workspaces','Fast frontend development/build; coordinated frontend and backend packages.','One repository and integrated application; Vite proxies /api to Express in development.'],
['Tailwind CSS 4 + shadcn/Radix + Motion + Lucide','Shared design system, accessible controls, subtle transitions and icons.','Keeps business pages consistent and usable on desktop and mobile.'],
['Node.js 22 + Express 5 + TypeScript','Authentication, API routes, validation, domain services and RDF transport.','Business rules stay on the server; the browser never sends SPARQL updates.'],
['OWL/RDF + SPARQL + Fuseki/TDB2','Formal domain vocabulary, linked facts, fixed queries and persistent graph storage.','Relationships are first-class RDF links and can be explored semantically.'],
['SQLite + Argon2id','Application users, sessions, setup tokens, rate limits and audit events.','Keeps identity/security data separate from insurance RDF.'],
['natural + Recharts + Cytoscape.js','French deterministic NLP, RDF-backed charts and ontology/individual graph.','Adds explainable query assistance and visual exploration without a generative API.'],
],[38*mm,62*mm,70*mm])]
story += [Spacer(1,3*mm),P('The key design split','Title2'),P('<b>Insurance business records live in Fuseki.</b> <b>Application accounts and sessions live in SQLite.</b> The original OWL file is preserved as the schema/reference source; the persistent Fuseki dataset is the runtime graph and can grow as managed records are created.','Callout'),PageBreak()]

# 3 Architecture
story += [P('2. Architecture and request flow','Title1'),P('The browser sends business fields, not RDF code. Express authenticates and validates them, applies domain rules, then calls a fixed query or update builder. Fuseki executes that operation against the configured dataset. Results return as RDF terms and are mapped into typed frontend models.'),table([
['Layer','What it does'],
['React + Router','Routes: /sinistres, /contrats, /assures, /experts, /dommages, dashboard, ontology, SPARQL Explorer and a floating NLP assistant.'],
['Typed API client + Vite proxy','Same-origin /api requests, JSON envelope, session cookies and CSRF headers for unsafe methods.'],
['Express middleware','Security headers, session lookup, CSRF and Origin checks, authentication and role permissions.'],
['Controllers / validators / services','Controllers stay thin; validators reject malformed inputs; services enforce ownership, references, revisions and deletion policy.'],
['SPARQL builders / repository','Allowlisted SELECT templates and generated conditional SPARQL Updates; no user-supplied query text.'],
['Fuseki + TDB2','Query/update endpoints over the persistent dataset; Shiro policy gates the endpoints.'],
],[42*mm,128*mm]),P('Read and write paths','Title2'),code('READ: React page -> GET /api/... -> Express session/RBAC -> service -> fixed SELECT -> Fuseki /query\nWRITE: React form -> POST/PATCH/DELETE JSON -> CSRF + role + write gate -> validation -> generated SPARQL Update -> Fuseki /update')]
story += bullets(['Lists use server-side search/filter/sort and bounded pagination. Pagination applies to distinct resource identities before optional RDF joins.','Updates use an application revision to detect stale edits. Conditional updates/readback help detect a no-op or conflict.','Delete rules prevent removing referenced resources; managed resources use metadata tombstones rather than cascading through the graph.','Fuseki admin UI access is deliberately restricted; application query endpoints are a separate capability.'])
story += [PageBreak()]

